content.text:
No errors. Let's force results to test UI. We can set race.player.lapsCompleted=2, sectors true, then teleport near finish and cross. But `updatePlayerProgress` uses `p.prevS` and p.sNorm. We can set car at sample index 0.88*N, set p.pos, p.yaw, vLong, vel; p.prevS = sNorm; then set gas true so it moves forward. It will cross within 1900*0.12=228m at 60m/s ~4s. Or place at 0.97 and go 50m -> 1s. Set sectors true and lapsCompleted=2. Race time maybe 60s. Then after crossing, finishRace -> results. Let's do:
```
const r=A.race,p=r.player,tr=r.track;
const idx=Math.round(tr.N*0.97);
const s=tr.samples[idx];
p.pos={x:s.x,z:s.z}; p.yaw=Math.atan2(s.tx,s.tz); p.vel={x:s.tx*45,z:s.tz*45}; p.vLong=45; p.vLat=0; p.prevS=0.97; p.sNorm=0.97; p.lapsCompleted=2; p.sectors=[true,true,true]; p.lapStart=r.time; r.locator.lastIndex=idx;
```
Then hold gas via setDemoInput. Wait 1.5s. Need ensure physics doesn't recover (offroad false). Then finish. Let's do and inspect results screenshot.

